\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Customer churn by contract type. Month-to-month customers account for the overwhelming majority of churned accounts.}}{14}{figure.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Average customer tenure in months by churn status. Churned customers have significantly shorter average tenure than retained customers.}}{15}{figure.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Customer churn by payment method type. Electronic check customers exhibit a disproportionately high churn rate compared to other payment methods.}}{16}{figure.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Customer churn by internet service type. Fibre optic customers churn at a higher rate than DSL or no-internet customers.}}{17}{figure.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Histogram of disconnection drivers. Competitor offerings, staff attitude, and general dissatisfaction are the most common reasons cited for customer departure.}}{18}{figure.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Distribution of customer churn score by churn status. The separation between active and churned customers confirms a distinct high-risk segment suitable for targeted intervention.}}{19}{figure.6}%
